  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One frame",
      "items": [
        "Each animation frame hands the Runner its wall time, capped at 100 ms, times the speed (0.5x, 1x, 10x)",
        "The Runner moves the shared traffic first, then every engine to the same simulated time, 50 ms at a time",
        "Past 12,000 events a frame ends early and the ledger says the run is slower than asked",
        "Each view carries every Variant's Snapshots, totals and ranked Findings to the panels"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Why the numbers are true",
      "items": [
        "The only clock is the simulated clock; the only randomness is three seeded streams",
        "Each Variant gets its own streams from the same seed, so one Variant's draws never shift another's",
        "Seed plus the control timeline replays the exact same run"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "An Attempt's life",
      "items": [
        "The Limiter allows or rejects; an allowed Attempt starts, queues or is shed at the Backend",
        "A timed-out Attempt keeps its Backend slot; that time is Wasted Work, which lets goodput collapse",
        "The engine measures busy and wasted slot time from the Backend into one Snapshot per simulated second",
        "The Retry Policy schedules the next Attempt on the event queue, or the Request ends"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Around the run",
      "items": [
        "The address bar holds Scenario, seed, Demand and Retry modes, so a copied link reopens the setup",
        "A seed or Retry change restarts the run from 0; the Demand slider and burst apply live",
        "Scenario notes explain what to watch and define each number"
      ]
    }
  ]
